# Bipartite lineage DAG + OpenLineage relay

This rule scopes AGENTS hard rule 48 + the Workstream A / B / C
additions from the Data Layer Selective Additive Enhancement.

## Architecture

- **Flat log (legacy, untouched)** — `data_lineage_events` keeps
  receiving rows via [`LineageWriter`](mdc:aqp/data/catalog/lineage.py).
  This is the OpenLineage outbox source; never replace it.
- **Bipartite graph (workstream A)** —
  [`lineage_dataset_vertex`](mdc:aqp/persistence/models_lineage_graph.py),
  `lineage_transform_vertex`, `lineage_edge`. Written by the
  [`BipartiteGraphObserver`](mdc:aqp/lineage/graph/observer.py)
  on the existing :class:`LineageBus`.
- **OpenLineage relay (workstream B)** —
  [`OpenLineageOutboxObserver`](mdc:aqp/lineage/openlineage/observer.py)
  writes `lineage_openlineage_outbox` rows; the Celery beat task
  [`drain_openlineage_outbox`](mdc:aqp/tasks/openlineage_relay_tasks.py)
  POSTs them to Marquez.
- **Signed transforms (workstream C)** —
  [`sign_transform_payload`](mdc:aqp/auth/signing.py) populates the
  `signature` + `signing_key_id` columns on `lineage_transform_vertex`;
  per-actor keys resolve via :class:`CredentialResolver`
  ([`signing_keys`](mdc:aqp/auth/signing_keys.py)).

## Hard rules

1. **Every Iceberg write captures snapshot metadata.**
   [`_emit_iceberg_lineage`](mdc:aqp/data/iceberg_catalog.py) MUST
   populate `details["iceberg_snapshot_id"]` and
   `details["iceberg_manifest_list"]` for the dataset vertex to be
   content-addressed correctly. Skipping this drops Iceberg datasets
   onto the fallback hash path.
2. **Bipartite emission is additive, never replaces the flat log.**
   The flat `data_lineage_events` log MUST keep writing so the
   OpenLineage outbox observer + audit downstream consumers keep
   working. The graph rows are a parallel projection.
3. **Edges are bipartite.** A `consumes` edge goes from a dataset
   vertex to a transform vertex; a `produces` edge goes from a
   transform vertex to a dataset vertex. Never mix these — the
   writer enforces direction.
4. **Signing follows rule 26.** Per-actor keys live behind
   :class:`CredentialResolver` under
   `CredentialKey("lineage_signing", "<actor_kind|user:id|agent:id>")`.
   Never hard-code key material in
   [`aqp/auth/signing.py`](mdc:aqp/auth/signing.py) or its callers.
5. **Public keys are archived.** Every issued signing key writes a
   `lineage_signing_key_archive` row via
   [`archive_public_key`](mdc:aqp/auth/signing_keys.py) so historical
   signatures stay verifiable after rotation.
6. **OpenLineage payloads are stable.** The
   [`aqp_event_to_openlineage`](mdc:aqp/lineage/openlineage/mapper.py)
   shape MUST conform to the OL `RunEvent` schema at
   https://openlineage.io/spec/. AQP-specific fields go under
   ``run.facets.aqp`` — never on the top-level keys OL reserves.
7. **Reads route through DataMCP.** Agents query the graph via
   [`data.lineage.ancestry`](mdc:aqp/data/mcp/tools/lineage_graph.py)
   and `data.lineage.impact`. Direct ORM imports from
   [`aqp/agents/`](mdc:aqp/agents) are forbidden (rule 22).

## Settings

- `AQP_LINEAGE_GRAPH_ENABLED` — toggle the bipartite observer.
- `AQP_LINEAGE_OPENLINEAGE_RELAY_ENABLED` — toggle the OL outbox
  observer + the Celery drain task.
- `AQP_LINEAGE_OPENLINEAGE_MARQUEZ_URL` — explicit Marquez endpoint;
  defaults to the topology-yaml entry when unset (rule 47).
- `AQP_LINEAGE_SIGNING_ENABLED` + `AQP_LINEAGE_SIGNING_MODE` —
  toggle signing + mode (off/permissive/strict).

## Don't

- Don't insert directly into the new tables. Go through
  [`LineageGraphWriter`](mdc:aqp/lineage/graph/writer.py).
- Don't shell out to Marquez with raw `httpx` calls outside
  [`relay.post_openlineage_event`](mdc:aqp/lineage/openlineage/relay.py).
- Don't add a new lineage `transform_kind` without also wiring the
  matching upstream → transform → downstream edge pair.
